<section class="sec pc-trust-problem pc-trust-problem--v37" id="problem" aria-labelledby="pcProblemTitle">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="pc-problem-simple reveal">
      <div class="pc-problem-simple__head">
        <span class="ey">The real PunchOut problem</span>

        <h2 id="pcProblemTitle">
          You are not worried about PunchOut.<br>
          You are worried about losing the customer.
        </h2>

        <p class="lead">
          When a bigger customer asks for PunchOut, four questions usually come to mind.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="pc-problem-simple__grid" aria-label="What suppliers are really asking">
        <article class="pc-problem-simple__card">
          <div class="pc-problem-simple__icon pc-problem-simple__icon--mint" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="/assets/ui-icons.svg#home-problem-connection" width="100%" height="100%"></use></svg>
          </div>
          <span class="pc-problem-simple__num">01</span>
          <h3>Will it work with my customer’s procurement system?</h3>
        </article>

        <article class="pc-problem-simple__card">
          <div class="pc-problem-simple__icon pc-problem-simple__icon--lavender" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="/assets/ui-icons.svg#home-problem-security" width="100%" height="100%"></use></svg>
          </div>
          <span class="pc-problem-simple__num">02</span>
          <h3>Can I trust it with an account this important?</h3>
        </article>

        <article class="pc-problem-simple__card">
          <div class="pc-problem-simple__icon pc-problem-simple__icon--peach" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="/assets/ui-icons.svg#home-problem-support" width="100%" height="100%"></use></svg>
          </div>
          <span class="pc-problem-simple__num">03</span>
          <h3>Who will help us get it live?</h3>
        </article>

        <article class="pc-problem-simple__card">
          <div class="pc-problem-simple__icon pc-problem-simple__icon--lime" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="/assets/ui-icons.svg#home-problem-monitoring" width="100%" height="100%"></use></svg>
          </div>
          <span class="pc-problem-simple__num">04</span>
          <h3>If something goes wrong, will we know?</h3>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="pc-problem-simple__close">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <strong>These are trust questions, not technical questions.</strong>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec pc-answer-simple" id="solution" aria-labelledby="pcSolutionTitle">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="pc-answer-simple__head reveal">
      <span class="ey">Here is our answer</span>
      <h2 id="pcSolutionTitle">Yes. And we make it simple.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        PunchOut Central is built to remove the risk behind each of those questions.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="pc-answer-simple__grid reveal" aria-label="How PunchOut Central answers supplier concerns">
      <article class="pc-answer-simple__card">
        <div class="pc-answer-simple__top">
          <span class="pc-answer-simple__check" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
          <span class="pc-answer-simple__num">01</span>
        </div>
        <h3>We connect to the systems your customers use.</h3>
        <p>cXML and OCI support connect procurement platforms to Shopify.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="pc-answer-simple__card">
        <div class="pc-answer-simple__top">
          <span class="pc-answer-simple__check" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
          <span class="pc-answer-simple__num">02</span>
        </div>
        <h3>You are not our first PunchOut customer.</h3>
        <p><strong>90+ customers</strong> use PunchOut technology built by our team, processing <strong>$50M+ in orders each year.</strong></p>
      </article>

      <article class="pc-answer-simple__card">
        <div class="pc-answer-simple__top">
          <span class="pc-answer-simple__check" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
          <span class="pc-answer-simple__num">03</span>
        </div>
        <h3>We help you get live.</h3>
        <p>Your standard integration is free. We help connect Shopify, configure the buyer, test the flow, and launch.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="pc-answer-simple__card">
        <div class="pc-answer-simple__top">
          <span class="pc-answer-simple__check" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
          <span class="pc-answer-simple__num">04</span>
        </div>
        <h3>You can see what is happening.</h3>
        <p>See sessions, purchase orders, Shopify orders, invoices, and issues from one place.</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="pc-answer-simple__proof reveal">
      <div class="pc-answer-simple__proof-copy">
        <span>Start with less risk</span>
        <strong>Beautiful. Easy. Affordable.</strong>
      </div>

      <div class="pc-answer-simple__terms">
        <span><b>✓</b> Free Integration</span>
        <span><b>✓</b> Cancel anytime</span>
        <span><b>✓</b> No transaction fees</span>
        <span><b>✓</b> From $500/month</span>
      </div>

       <a class="btn pri" href="https://app.punchoutcentral.com/platform/register" target="_blank">Connect my first buyer <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="sec pc-integrations" id="integrations">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head center reveal">
      <span class="ey">Integrations</span>
      <h2>Multiple procurement systems. One simple commerce connection.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Connect supported enterprise procurement environments through PunchOut Central while keeping Shopify as your commerce engine.
        Shopify is the supported commerce connector. BigCommerce and Magento are coming soon.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="pc-integration-lab reveal" id="pcIntegrationLab">
      <div class="pc-platform-palette" aria-label="Available platforms">
        <div class="pc-platform-group">
          <span class="pc-platform-group__label">Procurement</span>
          <div class="pc-platform-row" id="pcProcurementChoices"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="pc-platform-divider" aria-hidden="true">
          <span>↔</span>
        </div>

        <div class="pc-platform-group pc-platform-group--commerce">
          <span class="pc-platform-group__label">Commerce</span>
          <div class="pc-platform-row" id="pcCommerceChoices"></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pc-integration-guide">
        <span><b>1</b> Pick or drag logos</span>
        <i>→</i>
        <span><b>2</b> Drop them into either side</span>
        <i>→</i>
        <span><b>3</b> PunchOut Central connects the flow</span>
      </div>

      <div class="pc-integration-route" aria-label="Connection zone">
        <div class="pc-integration-side">
          <span class="pc-integration-side__label">Drop procurement here</span>
          <div class="pc-integration-drop" id="pcSourceDrop" data-accept="procurement">
            <div class="pc-integration-drop__selection" id="pcSourceSelection">
              <span class="pc-integration-drop__empty" aria-hidden="true">＋</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="pc-route-track pc-route-track--left" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="pc-route-packet pc-route-packet--forward"></span>
          <span class="pc-route-packet pc-route-packet--return"></span>
        </div>

        <div class="pc-route-hub" aria-label="PunchOut Central">
          <span>Managed gateway</span>
          <strong>PunchOut<br>Central</strong>
          <small>cXML · OCI</small>
        </div>

        <div class="pc-route-track pc-route-track--right" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="pc-route-packet pc-route-packet--forward"></span>
          <span class="pc-route-packet pc-route-packet--return"></span>
        </div>

        <div class="pc-integration-side">
          <span class="pc-integration-side__label">Drop commerce here</span>
          <div class="pc-integration-drop" id="pcDestinationDrop" data-accept="commerce">
            <div class="pc-integration-drop__selection" id="pcDestinationSelection">
              <span class="pc-integration-drop__empty" aria-hidden="true">＋</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pc-integration-foot">
        <span id="pcIntegrationSummary">Add platforms to both sides to start the connection.</span>
        <button class="pc-integration-reset" type="button" id="pcIntegrationReset">Reset</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="sec pc-order-process pc-order-process--v21" id="how" aria-labelledby="pcOrderFlowTitle">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="pc-order-process__head reveal">
      <div>
        <span class="ey">6 simple steps</span>
        <h2 id="pcOrderFlowTitle">From PunchOut to invoice. One connected order.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="lead">
        Your buyer shops. Their team approves. PunchOut Central keeps the order moving
        and shows you exactly where it is.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="pc-order-shell reveal" id="pcOrderFlow" aria-label="PunchOut order process">
      <div class="pc-order-progress pc-order-progress--integrated">
        <div class="pc-order-progress__main">
          <div class="pc-order-progress__action">
            <span class="pc-order-progress__pulse"></span>
            <div>
              <span class="pc-order-progress__kicker" id="pcOrderStepLabel">Step 1 of 6</span>
              <strong id="pcOrderStatus">Starting PunchOut session…</strong>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="pc-order-progress__metric" aria-label="Order completion percentage">
            <strong>
              <span id="pcOrderPercent">0</span>
              <span class="pc-order-progress__symbol">%</span>
              <span class="pc-order-progress__complete-label">Complete</span>
            </strong>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pc-order-route" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="pc-order-route__line">
          <span class="pc-order-route__fill"></span>
          <span class="pc-order-route__packet"><span></span></span>
        </div>

        <div class="pc-order-route__nodes">
          <span class="pc-order-route__node is-current" data-node="0"></span>
          <span class="pc-order-route__node" data-node="1"></span>
          <span class="pc-order-route__node" data-node="2"></span>
          <span class="pc-order-route__node" data-node="3"></span>
          <span class="pc-order-route__node" data-node="4"></span>
          <span class="pc-order-route__node" data-node="5"></span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pc-order-flow pc-order-flow--synced">
        <article class="pc-order-step" data-step="0">
          <div class="pc-order-step__icon" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64"><use href="/assets/ui-icons.svg#home-order-punchout" width="100%" height="100%"></use></svg>
    </div>
          <div class="pc-order-step__meta">
            <span class="pc-order-step__num">01</span>
            <span class="pc-order-step__check" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="/assets/ui-icons.svg#home-order-check-1" width="100%" height="100%"></use></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="pc-order-step__body">
            <h3>PunchOut Started</h3>
            <p>The buyer opens your Shopify catalog from their procurement system.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="pc-order-step__state">
            <span class="pc-order-step__state-dot"></span>
            <span class="pc-order-step__state-text">Waiting</span>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="pc-order-step" data-step="1">
          <div class="pc-order-step__icon" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64"><use href="/assets/ui-icons.svg#home-order-cart" width="100%" height="100%"></use></svg>
    </div>
          <div class="pc-order-step__meta">
            <span class="pc-order-step__num">02</span>
            <span class="pc-order-step__check" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="/assets/ui-icons.svg#home-order-check-2" width="100%" height="100%"></use></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="pc-order-step__body">
            <h3>Cart Returned</h3>
            <p>The cart and order details go back to the buyer’s procurement system.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="pc-order-step__state">
            <span class="pc-order-step__state-dot"></span>
            <span class="pc-order-step__state-text">Waiting</span>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="pc-order-step" data-step="2">
          <div class="pc-order-step__icon" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64"><use href="/assets/ui-icons.svg#home-order-approved" width="100%" height="100%"></use></svg>
    </div>
          <div class="pc-order-step__meta">
            <span class="pc-order-step__num">03</span>
            <span class="pc-order-step__check" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="/assets/ui-icons.svg#home-order-check-3" width="100%" height="100%"></use></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="pc-order-step__body">
            <h3>Buyer Approved</h3>
            <p>The buyer’s team reviews and approves the purchase in their procurement system.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="pc-order-step__state">
            <span class="pc-order-step__state-dot"></span>
            <span class="pc-order-step__state-text">Waiting</span>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="pc-order-step" data-step="3">
          <div class="pc-order-step__icon" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64"><use href="/assets/ui-icons.svg#home-order-po" width="100%" height="100%"></use></svg>
    </div>
          <div class="pc-order-step__meta">
            <span class="pc-order-step__num">04</span>
            <span class="pc-order-step__check" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="/assets/ui-icons.svg#home-order-check-4" width="100%" height="100%"></use></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="pc-order-step__body">
            <h3>PO Received</h3>
            <p>The approved purchase order arrives in PunchOut Central for a quick preview.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="pc-order-step__state">
            <span class="pc-order-step__state-dot"></span>
            <span class="pc-order-step__state-text">Waiting</span>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="pc-order-step" data-step="4">
          <div class="pc-order-step__icon" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64"><use href="/assets/ui-icons.svg#home-order-store" width="100%" height="100%"></use></svg>
    </div>
          <div class="pc-order-step__meta">
            <span class="pc-order-step__num">05</span>
            <span class="pc-order-step__check" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="/assets/ui-icons.svg#home-order-check-5" width="100%" height="100%"></use></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="pc-order-step__body">
            <h3>Store Order Created</h3>
            <p>PunchOut Central automatically creates the matching order in Shopify.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="pc-order-step__state">
            <span class="pc-order-step__state-dot"></span>
            <span class="pc-order-step__state-text">Waiting</span>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="pc-order-step" data-step="5">
          <div class="pc-order-step__icon" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64"><use href="/assets/ui-icons.svg#home-order-invoice" width="100%" height="100%"></use></svg>
    </div>
          <div class="pc-order-step__meta">
            <span class="pc-order-step__num">06</span>
            <span class="pc-order-step__check" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="/assets/ui-icons.svg#home-order-check-6" width="100%" height="100%"></use></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="pc-order-step__body">
            <h3>Invoice Generated</h3>
            <p>The invoice stays linked to the buyer and PO, with a quick preview in PunchOut Central.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="pc-order-step__state">
            <span class="pc-order-step__state-dot"></span>
            <span class="pc-order-step__state-text">Waiting</span>
          </div>
        </article>

      </div>

      <div class="pc-order-process__close">
        <div>
          <strong>Six steps. One connected order.</strong>
          <span>PunchOut Central handles the technical flow so you can focus on the customer.</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pc-order-celebration" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="pc-order-celebration__card">
          <span class="pc-order-celebration__eyebrow">Order Completed</span>
          <h3>You hit the SIXER!</h3>
          <p>
            Congratulations. Your order moved through all six steps.
            <strong>That’s how easy PunchOut can feel.</strong>
          </p>

          <button class="pc-order-restart" id="pcOrderRestart" type="button" aria-label="Replay the order journey">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/assets/ui-icons.svg#home-order-replay" width="100%" height="100%"></use></svg>
            <span>Replay the order</span>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pc-order-confetti" id="pcOrderConfetti" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" id="control">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head center reveal">
      <span class="ey">Everything in one place</span>
      <h2>One place for every buyer and store.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Manage multiple enterprise buyers, procurement platforms and Shopify stores without jumping between disconnected integrations.</p>
    </div>

    <figure class="buyers-shot reveal">
      <picture>
        <source srcset="/assets/buyers.avif" type="image/avif">
        <source srcset="/assets/buyers.webp" type="image/webp">
        <img
          src="/assets/buyers.jpg"
          alt="PunchOut Central overview showing connected stores, buyer connections, procurement networks, and live buyer status"
          width="3128"
          height="1376"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </picture>
    </figure>
  </div>
